{
  "id": "remint-deck-items",
  "title": "Re-mint: words mined into an existing deck in the window stay in the deck",
  "covers": [
    "re-mint step 1c (SYNC.md 10.4): an e:<seq> deck item whose seq is the entry of a note created in the window is window-derived: re-minted, re-keyed n:<note> (8.5: the same item)",
    "an e:<seq> item put before its note was created is re-minted after the note (step-1 order)",
    "an e:<seq> item of a word with no window note stays a shared key: discarded",
    "an item_removed e:<seq> is re-keyed n:<note> only when E holds a re-keyed item_put of the same (deck, e:<seq>); otherwise it keeps e:<seq> and removes the shared row (a pre-window e:<seq> item whose entry was materialised in the window)",
    "a re-keyed item_removed mints two removals, n:<note> and the original e:<seq>, so a key live before the window is removed too (pre-window e:2000008, re-put in the window, then removed)",
    "an item_put e:<seq> whose owner note is tombstoned in the window keeps e:<seq> (re-minted, not re-keyed)",
    "deck.item_put n:<window note> on an existing deck, and any item of a window deck: unknown_reference, re-minted unchanged"
  ],
  "narrative": [
    "A creates deck Mining and syncs (seq 1). A's clock jumps 10 days ahead; offline, A mines word 2000001 (note + card) into Mining with the canonical key e:2000001; puts e:2000003 into Mining and creates its note a minute later; puts e:2000009 (no note); adds a custom note N and puts n:N into Mining; creates deck Trip and puts e:2000001 into it.",
    "Before the window Mining also holds e:2000005 (seq 2). In the window A materialises entry 2000005 (note N5) and then removes the item: item_removed e:2000005. A mines 2000006 (note N6, put e:2000006) and removes it again. A mines 2000007 (note N7, put e:2000007) and then deletes N7. Mining also held e:2000008 before the window; in the window A materialises it (note N8), re-puts e:2000008 at position 4 (a reorder) and then removes it.",
    "Meanwhile B puts another word into Mining.",
    "Re-mint, removals and tombstones: the removal of e:2000005 has no re-keyed put of (Mining, e:2000005) in E, so it keeps e:2000005 and removes the shared row at the estimated time; re-keyed to n:N5 it would leave the live e:2000005 row and the word would reappear. The put of e:2000006 is re-keyed n:N6; its removal mints two removals, n:N6 and e:2000006 (the e:2000006 tombstone is a shared-row edit at the estimated time). Likewise e:2000008: the put becomes n:N8, the removal removes n:N8 and e:2000008, so the pre-window e:2000008 row is removed and the word does not come back. N7 is deleted in E, so its put keeps e:2000007 (re-keyed to a tombstoned note the item would be hidden).",
    "A pushes with the clock still wrong. The creations and the three e:<seq> puts into Mining are clock_ahead (Mining exists); card.created, the review, n:N into Mining and e:2000001 into Trip are unknown_reference.",
    "Re-mint: W = {both word notes, the card, N, Trip}. e:2000001 and e:2000003 in Mining are window-derived (their seqs are entries of notes in W): re-minted with keys n:<note>, which writes a window row and is the same item as e:<seq> by effective identity (8.5); e:2000003 is placed after its note. e:2000009 names no window note: discarded (shown in the discard list). n:N in Mining and e:2000001 in Trip write window rows: re-minted unchanged.",
    "A also reviewed the new card an hour after creating it (unknown_reference). It is re-minted in step 6b with a new id and reviewed_at shifted by the same delta as the creations, so it stays an hour after its card. `remint` lists the inputs; tools/validate.py recomputes the selection and the shift."
  ],
